stratford-uneven district council is  currently consulting on a psyc  allocations plan  and we want to hear your views to follow  up on my previous video about reserve  sites here i discuss how we propose to  release them  the site allocations plan identifies  around 3 100 homes for reserve housing  sites  we don't want to release them all in one  go so sap 3 sets out a release mechanism  so that the sites can be released in  smaller batches or tranches  that more closely correspond with the  need  sites will be released following the  hierarchy establishing policy cs15 of  the core strategy  starting with stratford-upon-avon as the  main town moving to the main rural  centres and then down through the four  categories of local service village  we've also adjusted the density  assumptions and applied lower densities  to sites in the smaller villages  to help ensure that the focus of any  development is in the larger and more  sustainable locations the tranches are  set out in annex  3 of the site allocations plan now  bear with me because this is where it  gets a little complicated  within each of the tiers just mentioned  we have subdivided the settlements into  smaller tranches in order to better  manage the release of reserve sites  for the local service villages we have  taken account of those villages with a  made neighborhood plan that identifies  reserve sites  those villages that have already met  their indicative core strategy housing  numbers  and those villages that have  significantly exceeded their indicative  core strategy housing numbers  for the main rural centres we have taken  account of those villages with a main  new  vader neighborhood plan that identifies  reserve sites  unlike local service villages there are  no indicative housing targets for the  main rural centres  so reflecting national policy and the  role of smaller sites in terms of speedy  delivery  we've applied site-sized thresholds to  identify  the different tranches because of the  way the sites have been identified it is  also proposed to vary the tranches  depending on the purpose the sites are  needed for  so just to recap the way the release  mechanism works is that if the council  accepts that it needs to release reserve  sites it will in the first instance  start with those sites in  stratford-upon-avon town  if further sites are needed it will then  release sites in the main rural centres  working through the tranches as  necessary before moving on to the local  service villages  again working through the tranches in  order  we will confirm the need to release  sites and which ones based on up-to-date  information  about any infrastructure and delivery  constraints through decision of the  cabinet  reserve sites exist to meet for four  very different purposes  and none with the exception of  birmingham have yet been quantified or  confirmed  as such it is appropriate to ensure that  there is some reserve available for each  of the four purposes  for this reason the council is proposing  to cap any release to a thousand homes  in the first  instance if a purpose is satisfied by  fewer than a thousand homes  these would then be made available for  the remaining purposes  i hope that helps and our release  mechanism is now a little clearer  remember to find out more and have your  say go to www.stratford.gov dot uk  forward slash zappo
 

